  "id": "monocular",
  "term": "monocular",
  "definition": "Monocular refers to something presented to or seen by only one eye rather than both eyes together. In the packet’s context, a monocular image is shown to one eye against a binocular background, which can create conflict between the eyes and affect visual performance.",
